---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/playbook';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How nakhapetov.com handles email subscriptions and anonymous analytics."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <section class="page-hero" style="padding-bottom: 2rem;">
    <div class="container prose-narrow">
      <p class="margin-note">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); max-width: 10ch;">
        Privacy
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="container prose-narrow">
      <p>
        Data controller: <strong>NAKHAPETOV ARTEM PE (sole proprietorship), Armenia</strong>. Contact:
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        If you request the free chapter, we collect your email address so we can send the chapter and related playbook messages (including an optional early-access demand form: a fair-price range and an optional comment). We also collect anonymous usage statistics (page views and button clicks) through PostHog. We do not send email addresses or form comment text to analytics.
      </p>

      <h2>Why</h2>
      <p>
        Email is used only for the playbook double opt-in, the free chapter, and demand / early-access signals before sales open. Analytics help understand which projects people open. Analytics run with in-memory persistence (no tracking cookies), so there is no consent banner for that.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
      <p>
        Email and mailing lists are handled by our email provider (Resend). The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Analytics are processed by PostHog. Confirm links use a short-lived signed token; we do not publish raw emails in URLs after confirmation.
      </p>

      <h2>How to unsubscribe</h2>
      <p>
        Every email includes an unsubscribe link. You can also write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and ask to be removed.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
